## Reusable content blocks (pull as needed)

### Hook variants for the opener

- **Generic PM**: "I bring product manager experience from end-to-end ownership of a live multi-tenant SaaS and a national platform strategy at the C-suite of a $100M+ turnover organisation, all underpinned by a strong technical understanding from my engineering background."
- **Domain-anchored** (e.g. mass-participation sport, federated org): "I bring product manager experience already exercised at the national level of a [DOMAIN], a personal history inside that kind of organisation as [participant, volunteer, leader], all underpinned by a strong technical understanding from my engineering background."
- **B2B SaaS-specific**: "I bring product manager experience earned through end-to-end ownership of a multi-tenant B2B SaaS and stakeholder and strategy work at the C-suite of a national federated organisation, all underpinned by a strong technical understanding from my engineering background."

### LIMSOC paragraph (proven phrasing)

> I act as product manager for LIMSOC, a mission-critical incident management system used across the country. My most recent engagement was an independent consulting piece authoring the platform's national scaling strategy and presenting it directly to the national executive.

Optional extensions depending on JD:

- **Discovery/business case focus**: "covering discovery across the federation, opportunity sizing for a national investment, and the business case to support it"
- **Documentation/roadmap focus**: "covering stakeholder requirements, product documentation, roadmap and national vision, and the testing and release coordination that goes with it"
- **Multi-jurisdiction scale**: "across eight jurisdictions with divergent operational requirements"

### Water safety review (use sparingly)

> I also led a national review on the policy at the core of Surf Life Saving Australia's purpose, our water safety policy, bringing every state into the room and into agreement on the foundations to continue improving towards our vision.

Include only when the JD specifically values multi-state stakeholder alignment under disagreement. Skip for most B2B SaaS roles — the LIMSOC paragraph already carries the federated stakeholder load.

### AccessBuddy block (B2B SaaS framing)

> I designed and shipped AccessBuddy, a multi-tenant SaaS live in production with real users, running as a solo founder at the velocity of a small team. I owned it end to end, from schema and API design through to OAuth and integration patterns, GCP deployment, observability, and the customer-facing product itself.

### AccessBuddy block (consumer/general framing)

> Outside paid work I designed and shipped AccessBuddy, a multi-tenant SaaS now live in production with real users, running as solo founder.

### The "comfortably hold both" sentence (CRUCIAL — always include)

> I can comfortably hold both business strategy and technical conversations, and translating between the two is where I add the most leverage [to a product team].

Variants depending on context:
- "...is one of the things I do best."
- "...is where I add the most leverage."
- "...is where I add the most leverage to a product team."

### Transferable engineering disciplines (use when JD wants engineering depth)

> Years of breaking complex problems into structured pieces, weighing trade-offs around scale and reliability, designing APIs for the long run, and instrumenting systems so the data tells the truth, are the disciplines I would bring into [JD-specific environment, e.g. shaping product decisions and partner integrations at COMPANY].

### Analytical lens (use when JD wants data/analytical mindset)

> The data side of engineering (schemas, instrumentation, pulling insight from usage data) is native territory, and that is the analytical lens I would bring to user feedback, market research, and the product calls those signals shape.

### Motivation paragraph templates

- **For a domain you know**: "What I want now is the broader scope and impact the product seat gives, and [COMPANY] is where I want to do that. [BELIEF SYSTEM SENTENCE about the domain]. That is the belief system I have spent my [LIFESAVING / X] career on, just in a different [SPORT / DOMAIN]. [COMPANY]'s framing of [DRAW SPECIFICS FROM JD] is one I recognise from the inside."
- **For a product you find interesting**: "What I want now is the broader scope and impact the product seat gives, and [COMPANY] is where I want to do that. The product surface ([SPECIFIC SCALE — e.g. 1,500 brand partners and six million customers worldwide]) is genuinely interesting, and the skills the JD calls for map directly to the work I have been doing. This is the role I would want to keep building that craft in."

