## Tailoring checklist

Before submitting, run through this:

- [ ] Role and company name correct in opener (no copy-paste errors)
- [ ] At least 2 JD keywords woven into the body (paste a line from the JD verbatim if it fits)
- [ ] Company-specific motivation paragraph has concrete numbers or mission framing, not generic
- [ ] No em dashes, semicolons, or colons anywhere in prose
- [ ] No comparative language ("few applicants", "most candidates")
- [ ] Word count under 450 (target 350-420 for one page)
- [ ] Closing line is "I look forward to the opportunity to discuss the role further with you." (or "Thanks for considering my application." for shorter/casual contexts)
- [ ] Sign-off: name + phone + email
- [ ] If recruiter-placed: separate test-the-water email drafted with honest gap acknowledged
- [ ] Export PDF using a font and toolchain that produces clean ATS-extractable text (test by copy-pasting "participation" or "multi-tenant" from the PDF — should paste cleanly, not as "par=cipa=on" or "mulA-tenant")

